#: processes/sdlc/qa-publish.bpmn:162
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`gh pr list --state all`: number, state and when it closed, so each `pr/<n>/` entry can be judged against its close date. A PR missing from the list is `unknown`, and an unknown is kept."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/qa-publish.bpmn:83
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`needs: gates` with `always()`: the publish runs whether the gates were green or red, because the evidence of a red commit is evidence too. The gates' result is carried into the manifest."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/qa-publish.bpmn:88
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`qa:publish --github` reads the event: a push to main publishes under `main/<sha>/`, a pull request under `pr/<n>/<head-sha>/` — the head that was tested, not the merge ref. It also reads whether the token can write, which the gateway after it routes on."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/qa-publish.bpmn:157
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A `schedule` trigger that actually fires — the lake-cache prune it was modelled on is guarded on `push` inside a dispatch-only workflow and has never run. A dispatch is a dry run unless `apply` is ticked."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/qa-publish.bpmn:97
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A fork PR's token is read-only (spike `3ds9`). That is decided from the event, not by attempting a push and reading the failure, so the skip is a stated outcome rather than a red run that means nothing."
msgstr ""

